From 17b4e2de98d1075e1f7c7496d2892f8fad0f737e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ThePlexus <31340423+ThePlexus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Mar 2026 13:28:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mb/cwwk/adl: add CW-ADLN-NAS Twin Lake variant support

Add support for the CWWK CW-ADLN-NAS Twin Lake variant.

CWWK CW-ADLN-NAS Intel Core 3 N355 has 1x DDR5 SO-DIMM slot, 6x
SATA 6Gbps, 4x 2.5GbE Intel i226 Ethernet ports, 2x M.2 NVMe 2280
slots and 1x PCIe slot. The second M.2 slot shares lanes with the PCIe
slot.

This variant needs LPSS UART0 console routing, and a board-specific
VBT for display bring-up.

Fan control uses the standard IT8613E Smart Auto path; this patch only
provides the board-specific channel and curve configuration required to
avoid full-speed fallback.

The shared src/mainboard/cwwk/adl/data.vbt is the older vendor-derived
VBT used by the existing Alder Lake CWWK variants and does not bring up
HDMI correctly on this board. Add a variant-local VBT extracted from
the known-good vendor firmware for board ID CWRADLNB0, BIOS version
05.27.00.01, built 2024-11-16 13:44:14, and use it for this variant.

Disable SeaBIOS PS/2 probing since this system has no PS/2 port.

TEST=Flash and boot on CW-ADLN-NAS Twin Lake (Core 3 N355, 32GB
DDR5-5600 OM32G55600SO2RX8NE11); verified LPSS UART console, HDMI
output, Displayport Output, four i226 NICs, primary NVME port, PCI bus
shows native SATA and JMB58x SATA, TCSS USB-C controller enumeration,
fan control, Intel PTT with CRB TPM and measured boot and SeaBIOS boot

Change-Id: I256cad8bdf99ec7881c72d946e6705005075b9f5
Signed-off-by: ThePlexus <31340423+ThePlexus@users.noreply.github.com>
